<title>BRAZIL: Brazil federation cuts state soybean figure-report.</title>
<headline>Brazil federation cuts state soybean figure-report.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian state of Rio Grande do Sul is now expected to produce 4.6 million tonnes of soybeans, down from an original forecast of 5.7 million, because of a prolonged drought, a local newsagency said.</p>
<p>According to the Fecotrigo cooperative federation, the loss to the region is in the order of 350 million reais ($330 million), Agencia Estado said.</p>
<p>In April, Fecotrigo had put the state crop at just below five million tonnes in anticipation of a crop loss of just over 790,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
